      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Darker skin tones can significantly alter the presentation of dermatologic conditions compared to lighter skin. For example, erythema in darker skin may appear more as hyperpigmentation or dusky patches rather than bright redness. Skin cancers, particularly melanoma, are notorious for presenting atypically in Black patients, often appearing as dark, brown, or black macules or patches rather than the classic sun-damaged lesions seen on lighter skin. Being aware of these pigmentary variations is crucial for accurate diagnosis in diverse populations.",
